  "details": "When creating menus with similar or identical layouts but different functions, it can sometimes be confusing what menu you entered (especially if the action menu was dismissed for sometime and you forgot where were, or if your controller suffers from stick drift).\n\nA solution to this would be to display additional text indicating what the current menu may be used for, a \"header\", centered within the menu, this is currently possible to do with some formatting tricks on odd-numbered expression menus, but requires trial and error to line up correctly with different text (and also gets misaligned once the button is hovered over, see last attached image), a properly built-in implementation would be ideal.",
